    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a draft excerpt focusing on struggle and hope. \"For too long, the sacred ground of our lives has been fenced off by the whims of the few. They hoard light while we shiver in shadow, claiming ownership over the very air we breathe. The Commonality calls for the dismantling of these gilded cages, to reclaim what is inherently ours—everything—and build a world where every hand feeds, and every soul belongs to the whole.\" This sets a dramatic tone while firmly establishing the core tenets of abolition and communal ownership.",
