      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Frame the opposition not as defenders of liberty, but as enslavers draped in the language of \"rights.\" Argue that their insistence on private ownership is merely the justification for institutionalized scarcity and the suffering of the masses. Contrast their \"freedom\" to accumulate with the true freedom of a society unbound by want. This narrative reframes property rights as relics of an abusive, old order that impedes true human flourishing.",
